hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15958","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said, Sufyan informed us, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from Abd Allah ibn Thabit, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I passed by a brother of mine of Banu Qurayza, and he wrote for me compendia from the Torah; shall I not present them to you? He said: The face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed. Abd Allah said: So I said to him: Do you not see what is on the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So Umar said: We are pleased with Allah as Lord, and with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as Messenger. He said: So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was relieved. Then he said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, had Musa become among you then you followed him and left me, you would have gone astray. You are my share of the nations, and I am your share of the prophets."
